<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:54:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d68e616aab0f56ae957eb5071994a0b7620bd99d6c4774bc4f627b64b1f9ffb8</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:54:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany expresses optimism over Montenegro's EU ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90997b5dbc8be92423b9f1d46964e1a9f7225d34d0c95e1cfa2a6f1508e102de</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-expresses-optimism-over-montenegro-s-eu-ambitions/a-79504069--d7fc739855e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-expresses-optimism-over-montenegro-s-eu-ambitions/a-79504069?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top diplomat said Montenegro has made "remarkable progress" in the accession process. The small Balkan state is being seen as a frontrunner among six regional candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz lauds NATO with Westphalian Peace Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11692dd31866f3ccf67bbe0448f1cdbfa26eb224cb59a2d94fd302bd1c5bcf92</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-lauds-nato-with-westphalian-peace-prize/live-79496180--2a3d5eea8753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-lauds-nato-with-westphalian-peace-prize/live-79496180?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a ceremony to honor NATO, the German chancellor warned that Russia will threaten the rest of Europe if it isn't stopped in Ukraine. In other news, the German military will set up its first drone regiment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany raises Deutschlandticket price to €66.80 a month from 2027 under new cost-based formula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd0f7d1502d77bee8b940699a9421df4071bea56e17aadfb6b3b9b26307c59d3</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-_66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524--e67f73547557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-€66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new cost-based formula has pushed up the price of Germany's nationwide public transport pass for 2027.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen ends collective wage agreements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ea2203dd5a42a9555e22335fe70001a23e0e5da983a894c5c30a95594bb1f9a</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802--2228595954e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an effort to cut costs, automaker Volkswagen terminated most of its collective wage agreements in Germany. This could reignite disputes with employee representatives.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germans' biggest fear is the high cost of living, an annual study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2e63afa40589d76b387339a8ab010b5cc4a12711f59a2c6bd292b44159720c5</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762--40495e454721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What do Germans fear most in 2026? Wars? Global crises? Wrong. Their biggest concern is the cost of living, which keeps rising.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany debates alleged antisemitism in the Left Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8b956433b28960f6f81597d36ae0712e1fc33a29b8c2300fd9c083f8b2c345c</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282--492f53fcd817.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Central Council of Jews in Germany thinks the Left Party is dangerous. Other Jews, however, are showing solidarity with the party. How does that add up?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>AI: Concern as Germany plans to double data center capacity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecedd008089d1e1f835c8efeed519dedc286f476c6328187f2d0e66787da70ef</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981--ddf2b388dfde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is rewriting the rules to attract data center investment from AI companies. But local communities are becoming increasingly skeptical.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3